{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `handler.go`.\n\nAdd the 'time' package to imports and print the current time in main"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Hello\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_653b18cf0e08"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Time:\\\", time.Now())\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_0e1209bbe4ac"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `sample.txt`.\n\nDelete line 3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\nLine 4: Fourth line", "tool_call_id": "call_155e2f9f5b3f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: First line\\nLine 2: Second line\\nLine 4: Fourth line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_b6455a43c54d"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `main.go`.\n\nAdd error handling to the processData function: return an error if data is empty, and update main to handle the error"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc processData(data string) {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Processing:\", data)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tprocessData(\"test\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_9b3ae8f5b09f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc processData(data string) error {\\n\\tif data == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"data cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Processing:\\\", data)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := processData(\\\"test\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Error:\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_06d1e4a5d838"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `README.md`.\n\nUpdate the code block: add a name parameter with default 'World' and use an f-string in the print statement"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Example\n\nHere's some code:\n\n```python\ndef hello():\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\n", "tool_call_id": "call_b0978a5bf615"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\", \"contents\": \"# Example\\n\\nHere's some code:\\n\\n```python\\ndef hello(name=\\\"World\\\"):\\n    print(f\\\"Hello, {name}\\\")\\n```\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_642aef56f791"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `handler.py`.\n\nAdd a reset method to the Calculator class that sets result to 0 and returns it"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "class Calculator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.result = 0\n    \n    def add(self, value):\n        self.result += value\n        return self.result\n", "tool_call_id": "call_dd8f9d786d6f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.py\", \"contents\": \"class Calculator:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n    \\n    def add(self, value):\\n        self.result += value\\n        return self.result\\n    \\n    def reset(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n        return self.result\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_92f5f40ae5a2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
