{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `docker-compose.yaml`.\n\nSet cache to true, add analytics: true under features, and set debug to false"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docker-compose.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "app:\n  features:\n    auth: true\n    cache: false\n  settings:\n    debug: true\n", "tool_call_id": "call_325ea81d8e7e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docker-compose.yaml\", \"contents\": \"app:\\n  features:\\n    auth: true\\n    cache: true\\n    analytics: true\\n  settings:\\n    debug: false\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_4a7d0034be73"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `validation.rego`.\n\nAdd a condition to exclude skipped tasks from the deny rule: add 'not task.status == \"Skipped\"' before the result assignment"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package example\n\nimport rego.v1\n\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome task in input.tasks\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Task %s did not succeed\", [task.name])\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_cd8577a48f8e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\", \"contents\": \"package example\\n\\nimport rego.v1\\n\\ndeny contains result if {\\n\\tsome task in input.tasks\\n\\ttask.status != \\\"Succeeded\\\"\\n\\tnot task.status == \\\"Skipped\\\"\\n\\tresult := sprintf(\\\"Task %s did not succeed\\\", [task.name])\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_a4524e270e1d"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
