{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `main.py`.\n\nAdd a reset method to the Calculator class that sets result to 0 and returns it"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "class Calculator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.result = 0\n    \n    def add(self, value):\n        self.result += value\n        return self.result\n", "tool_call_id": "call_1028de0e412b"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\", \"contents\": \"class Calculator:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n    \\n    def add(self, value):\\n        self.result += value\\n        return self.result\\n    \\n    def reset(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n        return self.result\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_1c588186b45f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only create the content the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- If a file doesn't exist, use write_file to create it"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `test.txt` with the following content:\n\n# My Document\n\nThis is a new document.\n\n## Section 1\n\nContent here.\n\n## Section 2\n\nMore content.\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file with the specified content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"test.txt\", \"contents\": \"# My Document\\n\\nThis is a new document.\\n\\n## Section 1\\n\\nContent here.\\n\\n## Section 2\\n\\nMore content.\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_fba9c16bea94"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
