{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `validation.rego`.\n\nAdd a condition to exclude skipped tasks from the deny rule: add 'not task.status == \"Skipped\"' before the result assignment"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package example\n\nimport rego.v1\n\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome task in input.tasks\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Task %s did not succeed\", [task.name])\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_e782a1f89b98"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"validation.rego\", \"contents\": \"package example\\n\\nimport rego.v1\\n\\ndeny contains result if {\\n\\tsome task in input.tasks\\n\\ttask.status != \\\"Succeeded\\\"\\n\\tnot task.status == \\\"Skipped\\\"\\n\\tresult := sprintf(\\\"Task %s did not succeed\\\", [task.name])\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_64b947529c71"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `server.go`.\n\nAdd an 'Age' field of type int to the User struct"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"server.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\ntype User struct {\n\tName  string\n\tEmail string\n}\n\nfunc (u *User) String() string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"User: %s\", u.Name)\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_03efa4968fca"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"server.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\ntype User struct {\\n\\tName  string\\n\\tEmail string\\n\\tAge   int\\n}\\n\\nfunc (u *User) String() string {\\n\\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\\\"User: %s\\\", u.Name)\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_cbec24fadf55"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
